  "job_B8.1.7.2_20251003_114824": {
    "text": "De Libro Iudicum, Anglice.\n\u00c6fter \u00f0am \u00f0e Moyses, se m\u00e6ra heretoga, \u00fe\u00e6t Godes folc gel\u00e6dde of Pharaones \u00feeowette ofer \u00f0a\n& God hi eac sona h\u00e6\u00f0enum leodum let to anwealde, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan h\u00e6fdon heora geweald, swa\n\u00d0a funde he him sona sumne fultum \u00e6fre, & he hig ahredde of \u00feam re\u00f0an \u00feeowte \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00f0enra leoda\nHig n\u00e6fdon manne cyning him gecorenne \u00fea git, for \u00f0am \u00fee God sylf w\u00e6s heora wissiend \u00fea &\nWE willa\u00f0 nu secgan swutelicor be \u00feisum, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t Israhela folc \u00e6fter Iosuam for\u00f0si\u00fee, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6\u00feelan\nGod wear\u00f0 him \u00fea yrre for yfelum d\u00e6dum, & bet\u00e6hte hig Chusam, \u00feam h\u00e6\u00feenan cyninge, swa \u00fe\u00e6t hig\nHig \u00fea eft clipodon to \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, & he him asende sona his fultum; gesette him anne\nOn him w\u00e6s Godes gast, & he hig \u00fea gewissode & feaht wi\u00f0 \u00feone Chusan & hine ofercom sona \u00f0urh\n& hi sy\u00f0\u00f0an wunedon on fulre sybbe ealles feowertig geara, & Othoniel \u00fea geendode his dagas.\nEft \u00fea Israhel \u00e6fter his for\u00f0si\u00fee geeacnodon heora yfel & \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan God mid weorcum\nSe hig ofsloh swi\u00f0e & heora burh gewann & gewilde hig ealle, swa \u00fe\u00e6t hig him \u00feeowodon on\nHig clipodon \u00fea swi\u00f0e on heora geswencednisse to \u00feam heofonlican Gode, his helpes biddende, & he\n& he him brohte \u00fea lac.\n\u00c6fter heora spr\u00e6ce cw\u00e6\u00fe se Aoth him to: Eala \u00feu Engol cining.\nIc h\u00e6bbe \u00fee to secganne ures Godes \u00e6rende; uton gan onsundron; & hig sona eodon in to sumum\n\u00d0a abr\u00e6d Aoth bealdlice his swurd mid his wynstran handa & hine hetelice \u00feidde, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea hiltan\nEnglon se cining l\u00e6g \u00fe\u00e6r swa dead.\n& Aoth bleow bealdlice his horn & ferde mid fultume to gefeohte sona, & ofsloh tyn \u00f0usend\n& he \u00fea Moabiscan miclum geeadmette & hi under\u00feeodde his agenum \u00feeowte, & heora land \u00fea w\u00e6s\n\u00c6FTER Aothes for\u00f0si\u00f0e hi geeacnodon eft heora unrihtwisnysse & heora yfel ongean God.\n& he hig \u00fea bet\u00e6hte sumum gramlican cininge, Iabin gehaten.\nAnd he h\u00e6fde heora geweald ealles twentig geara, & hig yfele ofsette; & hig \u00fea clipodon on hira\n\u00d0a asende him God sumne heretogan to, Barac gehaten, & he \u00fea ferde mid tyn \u00feusend mannum to\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea se Barac, gebyld swi\u00f0e \u00feurh God, feaht him togeanes mid his fyrde swi\u00f0e.\n& God \u00fea af\u00e6rde \u00feone fors\u00e6dan ealdorman & ealle his meniu, \u00f0\u00e6t hig mihtlease flugon, & hig man\n& Sesirra arn of his agenum cr\u00e6te fram ealre \u00fe\u00e6re fyrde, geegsod \u00feurh God, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he werig becom\n& heo cw\u00e6\u00fe to him: Gang in, la leof, to urum getelde, ne ondr\u00e6d \u00fee nan \u00feing; He eode \u00fea inn\nHe w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e ofurnen & he e\u00f0ode swi\u00f0e; b\u00e6d him drincan & heo him bli\u00feelice sealde: behelode hine\n& he hire cw\u00e6\u00f0 to: Stand nu & beheald: gif her \u00e6nig man cume acsigende embe me, \u00f0onne andswara\n\u00d0a \u00e6fter litlum fyrste gel\u00e6hte seo wifman an \u00fe\u00e6ra teldsticcena & stop inn digollice, gesloh \u00f0a mid\n& Barac com sona, sohte \u00feone Sisara; wolde hine ofslean; \u00f0a clipode seo wimman cu\u00f0lice him to, het\nGod \u00fea geeadmette Iabin \u00feone cining \u00e6tforan his folce; & hig f\u00e6stlice weoxon & mid strangre mihte\n& HI \u00fea feowertig wintra wunedon on sibbe.\nWe secga\u00f0 nu eac \u00fe\u00e6t we singa\u00f0 be \u00feisum on urum sealmsange, swa swa hit sang Dauid \u00feurh \u00feone\nHw\u00e6t sind Godes fynd buton \u00fea fulan h\u00e6\u00f0enan & \u00fea leasan Cristenan, \u00fee hlyda\u00f0 ongean God & mid\nAc \u00fees sealm us seg\u00f0, hu him sceal getimian, swa swa \u00f0am eorgan Sisaran & \u00feam arleasan Iabine,\n\u00d0EOS racu us seg\u00f0, \u00fee we nu \u00e6r r\u00e6ddon, \u00f0\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t Israhela folc, \u00fee we embe spreca\u00f0, si\u00fe\u00fean\n\u00d0a hig miclum geswencton; & heora orf genamon & heora \u00e6ceras aweston & ealle heora bigleofan\n\u00d0a fleah \u00fe\u00e6t earme folc to fyrlenum muntum & behiddon hig on scr\u00e6fum, mid hungre gew\u00e6hte; \u00f0\u00e6t\nIsrahela folc \u00fea earmlice clipode to \u00feam heofonlican Gode, his helpes biddende.\n& he him foresceawode sumne heretogan, Gedeon gehaten, heora agenes cynnes; \u00f0am bebead God\nGOD hine \u00fea gestrangode, & he gegaderode sona \u00fe\u00e6t earme folc \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r aflogene w\u00e6ron, & ferde \u00f0a\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00fe God sylf to him: Swi\u00f0e micel folc \u00feu h\u00e6fst on \u00feinre firdinge to \u00feam gefeohte; l\u00e6t hi gecirran\n\u00d0a geceas Gedeon, swa swa him gewissode God, \u00fereohund wera mid him of eallum \u00feam werode.\n& God him s\u00e6de \u00fea: Ic sylf nu alyse eow on \u00f0isum \u00ferim hundrydum, & \u00fee on hand bet\u00e6hte \u00f0a\n\u00d0am folce w\u00e6s gewunelic \u00fe\u00e6t hi weredon byman on \u00e6lcum gefeohte & \u00fea bleowon swi\u00f0e; \u00f0a het\n& cw\u00e6\u00fe him si\u00fe\u00fean to: Swa swa ge geseo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ic do, do\u00f0 ealle endemes \u00e6fter me sona.\nHe tod\u00e6lde hi \u00fea on \u00ferim diglum floccum.\n& ferde nihtes to \u00fe\u00e6r heora fynd wicodon, begunnon to blawenne mid heora byman swi\u00f0e & slogon\nWear\u00f0 \u00fea af\u00e6red eall seo h\u00e6\u00f0ene fyrd \u00feurch heora blawunge & \u00f0\u00e6ra buca sweg.\n& God hi geegsode, \u00fe\u00e6t hi begunnon to sleanne \u00e6lc heora o\u00f0erne mid hira agenum swurde on \u00fe\u00e6re\nHi flugon \u00fea sume, ac him ferde \u00e6fter Gedeon swi\u00f0e ofsleande \u00e6fre, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r afeollon fif & \u00ferittig\n& twegen ealdormen eac, Horeb & Zeb, \u00f0\u00e6r feollon ofslagenne.\n& HIM \u00e6tflugon twegen ciningas, Zebee & Salmana, ac he sohte hi georne, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he hi gel\u00e6hte; &\nW\u00e6s \u00fea wuniende on fri\u00f0e feowertig wintra be Gedeones wissunge.\nBe \u00feisum we singa\u00f0 eac on \u00feam fores\u00e6dan sealme ongean Godes wi\u00f0erwinnan, \u00fee willa\u00f0 \u00e6fre\nHW\u00e6T \u00fea \u00e6fter fyrste \u00fe\u00e6t Israhela folc begunnon to geeacnienne heora ealdan synna mid edniwum\n& hine micclum gremedon, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he mid yrre hi on hand bet\u00e6hte \u00feam h\u00e6\u00f0enan leodscipum, se\nHi wurdon \u00f0a gehergode & gehynde forswi\u00f0e eahtatyne gear under heora handa, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hig earmlice\n\u00d0A ofhearmode Gode heora yrm\u00f0a sona, & him foresceawode sumne heafodman, Iepthae gehaten, &\nHe ferde \u00f0a mid fultume & heora fynd ofsloh, & hi God bet\u00e6hte to his anwealde, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea\n& HI wunodon on sibbe an & \u00f0ritig geara.\n\u00c6FTER \u00feisum fyrste hig fengon eft to gremienne \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan God on heora ealdan wisan mid\nAn man w\u00e6s eardigende on Israhela \u00feeode, Manue gehaten, of \u00f0\u00e6re m\u00e6g\u00f0e Dan: his wif w\u00e6s\nHim com \u00fea gangende to Godes engel, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t hi sceoldon habban sunu him gem\u00e6ne; Se bi\u00f0\nHeo acende \u00fea sunu, swa swa hyre s\u00e6de se engel, & het hine Samson, & he swi\u00f0e weoxs, & God\n& HE wear\u00f0 \u00fea mihtig on micelre streng\u00f0e, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he gel\u00e6hte ane leon be wege, \u00fee hine abitan\nHE begann \u00fea to winnenne wi\u00f0 \u00f0a Philisteos & heora fela ofsloh & to sceame tucode, \u00feeah \u00fee hig\n\u00d0a ferdon \u00fea Philistei for\u00f0 \u00e6fter Samsone & heton his leode, \u00fe\u00e6t hi hine ageafon to hira anwealde,\nHig \u00f0a hine gebundon mid twam b\u00e6stenum rapum & hine gel\u00e6ddon to \u00feam folce.\n& \u00f0a Philisteiscan \u00fe\u00e6s f\u00e6gnodon swi\u00f0e, urnon him togeanes ealle hlydende, woldon hine tintregian\n& he gel\u00e6hte \u00f0a sona sumes assan cinban \u00fee he \u00f0\u00e6r funde, & gefeaht wi\u00f0 hig & ofsloh an \u00feusend\n& cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him sylfum: Ic ofsloh witodlice an \u00feusend wera mid \u00fe\u00e6s assan cinbane.\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea swi\u00f0e of\u00feyrst for \u00f0am wundorlican slege & b\u00e6d \u00feone heofonlican God, \u00fe\u00e6t he him\n\u00d0a arn of \u00feam cinbane, of anum te\u00f0, w\u00e6ter, & Samson \u00fea dranc & his Drihtene \u00feancode.\nNu gif hwa wundrie, hu hit gewur\u00f0an mihte \u00fe\u00e6t Samson se stranga swa ofslean mihte an \u00feusend\nNis \u00feis nan gedwimor ne nan dwollic sagu, ac seo ealde gesetniss ys eall swa trumlic, swa swa se\n\u00c6FTER \u00feisum he ferde to Philistea lande in to anre birig on heora anwealde, Gaza gehaten.\n& hi \u00fe\u00e6s f\u00e6gnodon, besetton \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t hus \u00fee he inne wunude, woldon hine geniman, mid \u00feam \u00fee he ut\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Samson heora syrwunga undergeat, & aras on midre nihte tomiddes his feondum & genam\nHine beswac swa \u00feeah si\u00f0\u00f0an an wif, Dalila gehaten, of \u00feam h\u00e6\u00f0enan folce, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he hire s\u00e6de,\n\u00d0a ahsode heo hine georne mid hire ol\u00e6cunge on hwam his miht w\u00e6re?\nAnd he hire andwirde: Gif ic beo gebunden mid seofon rapum of sinum geworhte, sona ic beo\n\u00d0\u00e6t swicole wif \u00fea begeat \u00fea seofon rapas, & he \u00feurh syrwunge swa wear\u00f0 gebunden.\n& him mann cydde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r comon his find; \u00f0a tobr\u00e6c he sona \u00fea rapas swa swa hefel\u00fer\u00e6das, & \u00fe\u00e6t\nHe wear\u00f0 eft gebunden mid eallniwum rapum & he \u00fea tobr\u00e6c swa swa \u00fea o\u00f0re.\nHeo beswac hine swa \u00feeah, \u00fe\u00e6t he hire s\u00e6de \u00e6t nextan: Ic eom Gode gehalgod fram minum\n& heo let \u00fea swa.\nHeo \u00fea on sumum d\u00e6ge, \u00fea \u00fea he on sl\u00e6pe l\u00e6g, forcearf his seofan loccan & awrehte hine si\u00f0\u00fean;\n& \u00fea Philistei gefengon hine sona, swa swa heo hine bel\u00e6wde, & gel\u00e6ddon hine aweg; & heo h\u00e6fde\n\u00d0a weoxon his loccas & his miht eft on him.\n& \u00fea Philistei full bli\u00f0e w\u00e6ron, \u00feancodon heora gode, Dagon gehaten, swilce hig \u00feurh his fultum\n\u00d0a Philistei \u00fea micele fyrme geworhton & gesamnodon hi on sumre upflora, ealle \u00fea heafodmen &\n& Samson \u00f0a plegode swi\u00f0e him \u00e6tforan, & gel\u00e6hte \u00fea sweras mid swi\u00f0licre mihte, & sloh hi",
